---Options customizing the time based transfer schedule. Options are migrated from the original ScheduleOptions message.
---@class gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.TimeBasedSchedule
---@field endTime? string Defines time to stop scheduling transfer runs. A transfer run cannot be scheduled at or after the end time. The end time can be changed at any moment.
---@field startTime? string Specifies time to start scheduling transfer runs. The first run will be scheduled at or after the start time according to a recurrence pattern defined in the schedule string. The start time can be changed at any moment.
---@field schedule? string Data transfer schedule. If the data source does not support a custom schedule, this should be empty. If it is empty, the default value for the data source will be used. The specified times are in UTC. Examples of valid format: `1st,3rd monday of month 15:30`, `every wed,fri of jan,jun 13:15`, and `first sunday of quarter 00:00`. See more explanation about the format here: https://cloud.google.com/appengine/docs/flexible/python/scheduling-jobs-with-cron-yaml#the_schedule_format NOTE: The minimum interval time between recurring transfers depends on the data source; refer to the documentation for your data source.

---A specification for a time range, this will request transfer runs with run_time between start_time (inclusive) and end_time (exclusive).
---@class gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.TimeRange
---@field endTime? string End time of the range of transfer runs. For example, `"2017-05-30T00:00:00+00:00"`. The end_time must not be in the future. Creates transfer runs where run_time is in the range between start_time (inclusive) and end_time (exclusive).
---@field startTime? string Start time of the range of transfer runs. For example, `"2017-05-25T00:00:00+00:00"`. The start_time must be strictly less than the end_time. Creates transfer runs where run_time is in the range between start_time (inclusive) and end_time (exclusive).

---Represents a data transfer configuration. A transfer configuration contains all metadata needed to perform a data transfer. For example, `destination_dataset_id` specifies where data should be stored. When a new transfer configuration is created, the specified `destination_dataset_id` is created when needed and shared with the appropriate data source service account.
---@class gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.TransferConfig
---@field notificationPubsubTopic? string Pub/Sub topic where notifications will be sent after transfer runs associated with this transfer config finish. The format for specifying a pubsub topic is: `projects/{project_id}/topics/{topic_id}`
---@field nextRunTime? string Output only. Next time when data transfer will run.
---@field disabled? boolean Is this config disabled. When set to true, no runs will be scheduled for this transfer config.
---@field scheduleOptions? gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.ScheduleOptions Options customizing the data transfer schedule.
---@field dataRefreshWindowDays? number The number of days to look back to automatically refresh the data. For example, if `data_refresh_window_days = 10`, then every day BigQuery reingests data for [today-10, today-1], rather than ingesting data for just [today-1]. Only valid if the data source supports the feature. Set the value to 0 to use the default value.
---@field userId? string Deprecated. Unique ID of the user on whose behalf transfer is done.
---@field metadataDestination? gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.MetadataDestination The metadata destination of the transfer config.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Data transfer modification time. Ignored by server on input.
---@field state? gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.TransferConfigStateEnum Output only. State of the most recently updated transfer run.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the transfer config. Transfer config names have the form either `projects/{project_id}/locations/{region}/transferConfigs/{config_id}` or `projects/{project_id}/transferConfigs/{config_id}`, where `config_id` is usually a UUID, even though it is not guaranteed or required. The name is ignored when creating a transfer config.
---@field encryptionConfiguration? gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.EncryptionConfiguration The encryption configuration part. Currently, it is only used for the optional KMS key name. The BigQuery service account of your project must be granted permissions to use the key. Read methods will return the key name applied in effect. Write methods will apply the key if it is present, or otherwise try to apply project default keys if it is absent.
---@field emailPreferences? gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.EmailPreferences Email notifications will be sent according to these preferences to the email address of the user who owns this transfer config.
---@field error? gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.Status Output only. Error code with detailed information about reason of the latest config failure.
---@field displayName? string User specified display name for the data transfer.
---@field schedule? string Data transfer schedule. If the data source does not support a custom schedule, this should be empty. If it is empty, the default value for the data source will be used. The specified times are in UTC. Examples of valid format: `1st,3rd monday of month 15:30`, `every wed,fri of jan,jun 13:15`, and `first sunday of quarter 00:00`. See more explanation about the format here: https://cloud.google.com/appengine/docs/flexible/python/scheduling-jobs-with-cron-yaml#the_schedule_format NOTE: The minimum interval time between recurring transfers depends on the data source; refer to the documentation for your data source.
---@field dataSourceId? string Data source ID. This cannot be changed once data transfer is created. The full list of available data source IDs can be returned through an API call: https://cloud.google.com/bigquery-transfer/docs/reference/datatransfer/rest/v1/projects.locations.dataSources/list
---@field scheduleOptionsV2? gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.ScheduleOptionsV2 Options customizing different types of data transfer schedule. This field replaces "schedule" and "schedule_options" fields. ScheduleOptionsV2 cannot be used together with ScheduleOptions/Schedule.
---@field paramConfig? gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.ParameterConfig Optional. The config for values in `params`.
---@field datasetRegion? string Output only. Region in which BigQuery dataset is located.
---@field destinationDatasetId? string The BigQuery target dataset id.
---@field ownerInfo? gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.UserInfo Output only. Information about the user whose credentials are used to transfer data. Populated only for `transferConfigs.get` requests. In case the user information is not available, this field will not be populated.
---@field params? gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.DocumentMap Parameters specific to each data source. For more information see the bq tab in the 'Setting up a data transfer' section for each data source. For example the parameters for Cloud Storage transfers are listed here: https://cloud.google.com/bigquery-transfer/docs/cloud-storage-transfer#bq
---@field managedTableType? gcp.bigquerydatatransfer_v1.TransferConfigManagedTableTypeEnum The classification of the destination table.

